"azgor" <nowhere.10.azgor@spamgourmet.com> wrote:
>Why not?  Because then you could simultaneously have intrinsic speed,
>jumping, invisibility, displacement, protection, stealth...  Sounds
>_much_ too powerful to me.  Also, next people will want to be able to
>eat wands to learn spells or some other such nonsense.

You can already simultaneously have intrinsic speed, invisibility,
protection and stealth:
 * Speed from role advancement, self-directed zapping with wand of
   speed monster, or eating quantum mechanic flesh.
 * Protection from divine favour or eating rings.
 * Stealth from role advancement, divine favour, or eating rings.
 * Invisibility from eating rings or stalker flesh, self-directed zapping
   with wand of invisbility, or quaffing a blessed potion of
   invisibility.

Note, however, that intrinsic speed is only +33% compared to extrinsic
speed's +66%.

Knights, of course, get intrinsic limited jumping.

Intrinsic displacement would be ludicrously overpowered full stop (since
there is currently a non-zero tradeoff for wearing a cloak of displacement
vs. other cloaks), as would intrinsic MR and reflection.
